From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:56:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 052/638] blink: bind async iterable init arguments explicitly

AI_PHASE: Phase 3 - single-process headless shell

AI_STATUS: Blink async iterable binding methods now use their class-declared initialization argument types on every compiler.

ROOT_CAUSE: The public methods used an abbreviated function-template parameter pack before a fixed trailing ExceptionState reference. GCC correctly treated that pack as non-deducible, so a generated one-argument ReadableStream iterator call could not match.

FIX_REASON: Use the enclosing PairAsyncIterable or ValueAsyncIterable InitArgs pack directly; implicit conversion and forwarding remain intact, while the compiler no longer has to infer a pack in a non-terminal position.

SCOPE: Blink pair and value asynchronous iterable binding helpers

VALIDATION: Generated ReadableStream, FileSystemDirectoryHandle, and SharedStorage V8 binding objects compiled with the AROS GCC cross-toolchain; staged diff check passed.

RISK: Callers now convert directly to the class-declared InitArgs parameter types before dispatch, matching the virtual CreateIterationSource contract; current instantiations are pointers or empty packs.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap
---
 .../blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/async_iterable.h      | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

